---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/url';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, NETWORK_NAME } from '../../../site.config.mjs';
---

<SiteLayout title="Member code of conduct" membersFooter>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-12 md:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl">Member code of conduct</h1>
    <div class="prose-page">
      <p class="text-lg">
        The {NETWORK_NAME} brings together people from different disciplines, professions and career stages. Members are
        expected to follow this code when using the directory, sharing resources, contacting others or taking part in
        network activities.
      </p>

      <h2>Use and share resources responsibly</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Resources made available exclusively to members must not be forwarded, republished or shared outside the network without the resource owner’s permission, and only in line with any ethical requirements.</li>
        <li>Follow the licence and any conditions attached to each resource, including conditions on use, adaptation and redistribution. If permissions are unclear, ask the contributor before using or sharing it.</li>
        <li>Do not share your sign-in details or links that give others access to restricted resources.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Respect contributors and their work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Acknowledge the people or teams who created a resource when you use or adapt it.</li>
        <li>Only contribute materials you own or have permission to share. Identify their source and explain any restrictions on their use.</li>
        <li>Represent your expertise, affiliations and contributions accurately, and keep your directory information current.</li>
        <li>Discuss roles, contributions and expectations early in a collaboration, including authorship, acknowledgement and use of shared materials.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Protect participants and confidential information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Share blank templates only. Do not upload research datasets, completed consent forms, participant information or anything that could identify a participant.</li>
        <li>Do not share confidential institutional, clinical or research information without authorisation.</li>
        <li>Check resources against your own institution’s ethics and governance requirements before using them.</li>
        <li>Arrange research data access directly with the custodian and follow the applicable approvals and agreements. A directory listing does not grant permission to access or use data.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Treat others with respect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Be courteous and inclusive, regardless of discipline, profession, career stage, background or identity.</li>
        <li>Discuss differences constructively. Harassment, discrimination, bullying, intimidation and abusive behaviour are not acceptable.</li>
        <li>Use contact forms for genuine enquiries relevant to the network, including research, clinical, policy, education and collaboration opportunities.</li>
        <li>Do not use the network for unsolicited sales, marketing, bulk recruitment messages or repeated unwanted contact.</li>
        <li>Respect others’ decisions about whether to respond, collaborate or provide access to resources or data.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Raise concerns</h2>
      <p>
        Contact the leadership committee at <strong>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</strong> if you believe a resource has been shared
        without permission or someone has breached this code. Provide enough detail to explain the concern, without
        including sensitive material.
      </p>
      <p>
        Reports will be handled sensitively and shared only with those who need the information to assess or respond to
        the concern. Do not retaliate against someone for raising a concern in good faith.
      </p>
      <p>A committee member with a conflict of interest in a matter should not take part in reviewing or deciding it.</p>

      <h2>Responding to breaches</h2>
      <p>
        The leadership committee may request corrections, issue a warning, remove a listing or resource, restrict access,
        or suspend or end membership, depending on the nature and seriousness of the concern.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where appropriate, the person concerned will have an opportunity to respond before a final decision is made.
        Access or content may be restricted while a concern is reviewed.
      </p>
      <p><a href={withBase('/resources/')}>Back to resources</a></p>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
